# THE BUILD CONTEXT IS NOW THE REPOSITORY ROOT, so it has to be trimmed.
#
# render.yaml builds the API and workers with `rootDir: .` because the
# image must contain research/beta48/shadow -- the bridge imports the
# tested EV modules rather than carrying a copy. Without this file the
# context is ~271 MB (135 MB of it .git, 195 MB of it research/), all
# uploaded on every deploy, to ship ~7 MB that matters.
#
# WHAT MUST SURVIVE, and what proves it: backend/ and
# research/beta48/shadow/ are the only trees the Dockerfile COPYs.
# backend-image-check.yml builds this exact context and then imports
# every required module INSIDE the container, so an over-broad rule
# here fails CI rather than silently shipping an image whose bridge
# can never load.

.git
.github
**/.pytest_cache
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.DS_Store
**/node_modules
*.egg-info

frontend/
docs/
ops/
edge-engine/
pmus-broker/
rn1-collector/

# research/ is 195 MB and the image needs one 7 MB subtree of it.
# Everything is excluded, then that subtree is re-admitted -- each
# parent has to be re-admitted too, because Docker will not descend
# into a directory it has already excluded.
research/*
!research/beta48
research/beta48/*
!research/beta48/shadow
research/beta48/shadow/**/__pycache__
